 "observations": [
  "The page number «145» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 34», in bold sans serif, underlined. At the foot, the signature line of the printed sheet: «D. K. D. Vidensk. Selsk. Skr., 7. Række, hist. og filos. Afd. III. 1.» on the left and the sheet number «19» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. The titles (L01-L02), in bold, the sigla in roman; L02 in smaller bold type, with note 1. The folios of the manuscripts stand at the right of the titles in two lines, «C 59v, O 117r,» and «N 12r.», the letters raised; here as right margin notes. N's folio follows «N 29v.» of p. 144 (JP2 0176); pp. 146-147 (JP2 0178-0179) continue with «N 12v.» and «N 13r.».",
  "The table: rules and heads as on p. 144 (JP2 0176), with «Examinatio centri5)» and «Latitudo Jovis accedentis» over «prima» and «secunda» without a note. Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L03-L07), the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. L08, the units, in bold.",
  "L02 and note 1: the node in the title, 2s 12° 1′, is O's reading; C and N have 2. 22. 1, N adding 2. 12. 1 «secundum alios». The text (chapter 19, p. 15, JP2 0047) and the title of p. 144 (JP2 0176, L03) give 2s 22° 1′.",
  "L09-L38. Checked as on p. 144 (JP2 0176): the Sublimatio is 5s 22° 32′ less half the Examinatio argumenti in every row, a half minute counted as a whole, except at 38° and 56°. At 38° (L16), 5s 19° 39′ answers to an Examinatio argumenti of 5° 46′ or 5° 47′, where the table has 5° 48′; the steps of that column to and from 38°, 10′ and 7′, stand against 8′ or 9′ around them, and the equation of the epicycle gives 5° 46.0′. At 56° (L34) the edition prints 5s 28° 31′: see the critical note; 5s 18° 31′ stands for 5s 18° 31½′, with C's minutes (note a), where O and N have 32, the larger minute that the column gives everywhere else. No note of the apparatus bears on the 5° 48′ of 38°.",
  "L09-L38. The Examinatio argumenti agrees with the equation of an epicycle of radius 11.3 to within 1.6′ in every row except at 38°, 2.1′ above it; the thirty values of p. 144 agree with the same equation to within 1.3′. The Latitudo secunda is 2° 30′ · sin x to within 0.6″ in every row except at 41° and 58°: at 41° (L19), 1° 38′ 22″ is 2.5″ less than 1° 38′ 24.5″, with C's minutes (note e); at 58° (L36), 2° 7′ 19″ is 6.6″ more than 2° 7′ 12.4″, and its steps from 57° and to 59°, 1′ 31″ and 1′ 15″, stand against about 1′ 24″ and 1′ 22″.",
  "L09-L38, the other columns, compared from row to row: the Examinatio centri increases by 3′ to 5′ a degree, to 4° 25′ at 60°, and lies within 3.1′ below 5° 6′ · sin x; 5° 6′ · sin 60° = 4° 25.0′. The Statio prima increases by 1′ a degree from 4s 4° 18′ at 31° to 4s 4° 36′ at 49°; at 50° (L28) it has 4s 4° 39′, 3′ more than at 49° and 1′ less than at 51°, and then rises by 1′ or 2′ a degree to 4s 4° 53′ at 60°. No note of the apparatus bears on the 39. The Latitudo prima is 1° 28′ to 34°, 1° 27′ to 40°, 1° 26′ to 48°, 1° 25′ to 54° and 1° 24′ from 55° on.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked: the Sublimatio 5s 18° 28′ at 57° (note b, O, against C's 38) agrees with the rule; the Examinatio argumenti 7° 27′ at 51° (note c), 7° 27.3′ by the epicycle; the degree 2 of the Latitudo secunda from 54° to 60° (notes d-d, N, against the 1 of C and O) and its minutes 38 at 41° (note e, C, against O's 37) agree with the computation.",
  "L28, the seconds of the Latitudo secunda at 50°, «54»: the 4 is printed faintly. N02: the dash after «2. 12. 1 N» is printed in two pieces, 20 and 14 px long with a gap of 2 px; transcribed as one long dash. N05: the dash before e) is short, 17 px against 34-35 px, and is transcribed as an en dash. Italics: «om.». N01-N02: the ellipses «. . . .» of the lemmata as printed."
 ],
